0..89 Comment "// `Path.walk` computes on every filler that resolves, and stays stuck on a carried cell."
90..92 Comment "//"
93..165 Comment "// Nothing about a filler is primitive. A filler comes from completion\'s"
166..236 Comment "// derivation, from the filler generator or from a composite of cells."
237..239 Comment "//"
240..320 Comment "// `Path.walk` over a generated filler and over a composite of `Path.here` cells"
321..398 Comment "// reduces to its motive\'s base. The circle\'s `loop` stays stuck by name. The"
399..460 Comment "// row over completion\'s filler stands beside its derivation."
461..463 Comment "//"
464..531 Comment "// - see: `derived-rule.gandr` — the row over completion\'s filler"
532..599 Comment "// - see: `compose-chain.gandr` — unbiased composition of a chain"
601..639 Comment "// The circle, its point and its loop."
640..646 Keyword "import"
647..648 StringLit "\""
648..667 StringLit "./circle-base.gandr"
667..668 StringLit "\""
668..669 Other ";"
